messages:
alex.k: Hey team — Support wants LogRocket for web session debugging (session replay + network capture). They say it's important to reproduce UI issues. Any immediate redaction / approval concerns? cc @maria_s @dave_r

maria_s: Need to confirm no PII is captured (emails, SSNs, payment info). LogRocket supports input masking and request sanitizers. Do we have a standard redaction snippet we can reuse?

dave_r: We trialed LogRocket in the sandbox last year. By default it captures DOM + XHR bodies. We should treat it like an error-tracker + recording: whitelist what support can see. Off the top: mask inputs with selectors and strip network bodies.

alex.k: Support's ask: read-only access for support agents, limited to sessions with explicit customer consent. Also asked if retention can be 30 days. Thoughts?

security-bot: FYI — vendor risk assessment required for session-replay tools. See internal vendor approval docs: https://redwood.internal/docs/vendor-approval (includes checklist for SSO, retention, encryption, data residency).

maria_s: Also need Legal check for replay in EU and other regulated regions — some customers require opt-in. @sam.t can you confirm compliance constraints?

sam.t: Legal: session replay is permitted with clear consent and opt-out. For EU customers we need explicit consent and update to privacy policy. I'll loop in Legal and follow up.

dave_r: Implementation proposal (config sketch):
```js
LogRocket.init('redwood/web', {
  network: {
    requestSanitizer: (req) => ({
      ...req,
      body: undefined, // drop bodies by default
      headers: sanitizeHeaders(req.headers)
    })
  },
  dom: {
    inputSanitizer: (node) => {
      // mask values for email/ssn-like inputs
      if (matchesSelector(node, 'input[type="email"], input[name*="email"], input[name*="ssn"], input[id*="ssn"]')) return '***';
      return undefined;
    }
  },
  retentionDays: 30,
  enabled: true // later gate by consent flag
});
```

// mask utility: replace values for specific selectors and patterns before sending

maria_s: That looks reasonable. Add a global fail-safe: if `user.meta.consent === false` or `gdpr_optout === true` then disable recording for that session entirely. Also ensure server-side logs never echo full session payloads.

lisa_support: From Support: need a console role for read-only session access and audit logs showing who viewed which sessions. Can we require SSO + SCIM provisioning?

security-bot: Policy: vendors must support SSO (SAML/OIDC) and SCIM or provable least-privilege user management. Please include an access matrix in the vendor form describing roles, RBAC, and audit features.

alex.k: Action items: dave to add config + fail-safe redaction, sam to get legal signoff on EU/privacy, I will fill vendor risk form and request SSO/SCIM info from LogRocket. Any objections?

maria_s: No objections from sec. Also request encryption-at-rest confirmation and region of storage from vendor. :+1:

sam.t: On it — will update Legal signoff by EOD Wed 03/12.

lisa_support: Thanks — Support will wait to enable until SSO & audit are in place.

alex.k: I'll open the vendor form now and ping when done. :eyes:
